@startuml
title NetStrike CITEF example environment
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
actor "Participant / facilitator\nbrowser" as Browser
cloud "Internet" as Internet
node "Ansible control host\nlocation not specified" as Ansible
package "Cyber Range - exercise network\n10.77.0.0/24 | simcorp.test" as Exercise {
  node "DC01\n10.77.0.10\nWindows Server 2025 LTSC\nAD DS, DNS, NTP\nSplunk Forwarder, Sysmon" as DC
  node "CTRL01\n10.77.0.11\nUbuntu Server 26.04 LTS\nController / portal :8443\nIDP01, HELPDESK01,\nCLOUD01, FILE01\nSplunk Forwarder" as CTRL
  node "FIN-WS01\n10.77.0.20\nWindows 11 26H2\nWinRM, Splunk Forwarder,\nSysmon" as WS
  node "SPLUNK01\n10.77.0.30\nCyber Range Linux host\nSplunk Enterprise 10.0.1\nReceiver :9997" as SPLUNK
}
cloud "Management network\n10.77.1.0/24\nNo asset addresses specified" as Management
Browser --> CTRL : HTTPS :8443
Ansible --> DC : WinRM :5986
Ansible --> WS : WinRM :5986
Ansible --> CTRL : SSH :22
Ansible --> SPLUNK : SSH :22
CTRL --> DC : DNS :53\nNTP :123
WS --> DC : DNS :53\nNTP :123
SPLUNK --> DC : DNS :53\nNTP :123
CTRL --> SPLUNK : Splunk Forwarder :9997
DC --> SPLUNK : Splunk Forwarder :9997
WS --> SPLUNK : Splunk Forwarder :9997
Exercise ..> Internet : Egress denied
note bottom of Management
  The example defines this CIDR but does not assign
  addresses or interfaces to any hosts.
end note
note bottom
  Based on citef-config/environment.example.json.
  Logical connections are shown; firewall rules, routes,
  browser source addresses, and Ansible host placement
  are not specified by the example manifest.
end note
@enduml